What is PET Bottle Recycling?
PET bottle recycling comprises sustainable processes that transform post-consumer polyethylene terephthalate (PET) waste into reusable materials, playing a crucial role in circular economy initiatives. These solutions involve multiple stages including collection, sorting, washing, shredding, and advanced reprocessing techniques to convert PET waste into food-grade recycled PET (rPET) for packaging applications or polyester fibers for textile and industrial uses.
The industry has evolved significantly from basic mechanical recycling to incorporating advanced chemical recycling methods that can handle contaminated and multi-layer packaging. Major industry players such as Veolia, Indorama Ventures, and Plastipak are actively expanding their recycling capacities through strategic investments and partnerships to meet the growing demand for sustainable packaging solutions.
